`-Xlint:try` warns when AutoCloseable.close() may throw InterruptedException. Fix: make `close()` not declare InterruptedException — handle the interrupt inside:

```java
@Override public void close() {
    thread.interrupt();
    try {
        thread.join(TimeUnit.SECONDS.toMillis(30));
    } catch (InterruptedException interrupted) {
        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
        throw new IllegalStateException("interrupted while stopping the Host entry", interrupted);
    }
    assertFalse(thread.isAlive(), "...");
}
```

